// Jest Snapshot v1, https://jestjs.io/docs/snapshot-testing

exports[`runInit — backend section backend omitted equals backend 'none' — the post-rename baseline (regression) 1`] = `
"init (preset: solo, frontend: react-vite)

## add-fsd-lite
FSD layers (in web, apps/web/src):
  apps/web/src/app       composition root: providers, routing, global styles (the framework entry point lives here)
  apps/web/src/pages     one slice per screen, composed from the layers below
  apps/web/src/features  one slice per user-facing capability (add-to-cart, sign-in)
  apps/web/src/entities  one slice per business object (user, product)
  apps/web/src/shared    segments, not slices: ui, api, lib, model, config — named by purpose
Layer directories appear with their first slice (canonical FSD):
  nx g @clearlydev/nx-archweave:feature --name=<name>   (page, entity and shared work the same way; --segments=ui,api)
  widgets/ is outside the default scope but one command away: nx g @clearlydev/nx-archweave:widget
Imports go downward only, slices on one layer never import each other, and a slice is
imported through its index.ts — the archweave/fsd-boundaries ESLint rule reports violations.

ESLint: report-only (pass --applyEslint to write the rule into web's eslint.config.mjs).
// nx-archweave FSD layer rules — add these to the frontend app's eslint.config.mjs yourself:
// 1) the import after the last import,
// 2) the spread as the last element of the export default [...] array.
import { fsdBoundaries } from '@clearlydev/nx-archweave/eslint';
...fsdBoundaries({ severity: 'warn' }),

## add-agent-rules
add-agent-rules:
  hosts: claude-code
  locale: en
  teamRules: false

  CLAUDE.md: created

## add-github-templates
  .github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md: created

## add-review
  .github/workflows/claude-code-review.yml: created
  toolkit.config.json: created with the review field

Note: the review workflow stays green-skipped until you register the CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN secret.
Note: this workflow runs with elevated permissions only after it is merged to the default branch —
merging is the first real validation.

## toolkit.config.json
  recorded locale, preset, frontend, fsd.enforcement, agentRules.teamRules, aiHosts (updated)"
`;
